      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VITE MONET (4) looks close to a win after a series of good efforts from wide barriers, beaten only 1.3m here on Tuesday. Owns a good record at this longer distance and a better draw could see him back in the winners' list. MIKE ROSS NZ (2) has come from wider barriers at his last couple and hasn't been far away. Goes well at the longer trip and a low draw brings him into contention. DOM TORETTO NZ (1) backs up from Tuesday where he came from much deeper to be beaten 5m. That continued a run of wide barriers and he did manage to place prior. Much better served by the inside draw. MICHAYWEY (6) draws wider and goes up in distance but is hard to knock having placed in four of his last five outings. KANENA PROVLIMA (8) will enjoy a class drop off the Inter Dominion series where he was fifth in the consolation last week.",
